{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794425495,"nonce":"IO335JIbIInwUyNLO9t+n3vN3O4=","message":"Fixed in 9081e5e0f7859f9638bafc6a1de756e6f197dd54 (local main, not pushed).\n\nAfter a call returns, the SSA walker clears the slots of pointer-typed values that died at or before it. It is computed once per prepared body from liveness, with a forward pass over what is dead but still in its slot, so a value is listed at the first call after it dies: at its last use or on an edge that leaves its live range. `ASH_AIR_KILLS=0` turns it off.\n\nResults on the release binary:\n- hxn's program, live after 5 collections (200 expected): interp 200, hybrid 200, jit 200. With `ASH_AIR_KILLS=0`: 10200.\n- New test `dead_call_results` (fixture TestDeadCallResults.hx, descriptor limit 160): passes in interp and hybrid; fails on the previous binary and with `ASH_AIR_KILLS=0`.\n- Unit conformance, interp and hybrid: 1069/1069 cases, 10971/10971 assertions, no uncounted rows. ash_interp unit tests, finalizers, osr_retier (7), hot_reload (31), process_pipe_gc, heap_census, gc_dump_marks, closure_equality, ref_args, null_bound_closure all pass.\n- Overhead, interp with clearing on vs off, median user CPU of four interleaved runs at load 50-70 (noisy, Mac, not confirmed on the NUC): bench_free_call +0.7%, bench_binary_trees +0.7%, bench_method_call +2.6%; run-to-run spread within one arm was larger.\n\nRemaining gaps are in the follow-up issue.","files":null}]}